WEBVTT

00:00:05.070 --> 00:00:05.860
Okay!

00:00:09.610 --> 00:00:10.740
Aoi-san.

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:12.990
Y-Yes?

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:35.430
<b>Holmes of Kyoto</b>

00:01:46.580 --> 00:01:51.590
Episode 7

00:01:46.580 --> 00:01:51.590
Straying and Enlightenment

00:01:57.140 --> 00:01:59.260
So, Rikyu,

00:01:59.260 --> 00:02:01.920
to what do we owe this casual visit?

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:02.970
You know what!

00:02:03.290 --> 00:02:06.480
I just can't leave Kura in Aoi-san's hands.

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:11.970
She's not a suitable partner for you.

00:02:11.970 --> 00:02:16.240
I can't have you talkin' that way
 about Aoi-san in front of me.

00:02:16.840 --> 00:02:19.530
Kiyo-nii... You're so cool.

00:02:21.970 --> 00:02:24.590
Aoi-san, why don't we take a break?

00:02:25.540 --> 00:02:26.420
Aoi-san?

00:02:27.030 --> 00:02:28.500
R-Right!

00:02:31.740 --> 00:02:34.340
Here. I made some for you, too.

00:02:34.970 --> 00:02:36.380
Thank you.

00:02:36.790 --> 00:02:40.520
The black tea Rikyu makes 
is very fine indeed.

00:02:40.520 --> 00:02:42.140
Is it?

00:02:42.390 --> 00:02:43.900
And it's not just his black tea.

00:02:43.900 --> 00:02:46.500
He's skilled at brewing all kinds of tea.

00:02:48.990 --> 00:02:51.030
You're not shaming the Rikyu name, I see.

00:03:00.030 --> 00:03:01.210
It's delicious.

00:03:01.990 --> 00:03:04.530
Well... thanks.

00:03:13.520 --> 00:03:16.100
You appear rather listless today.

00:03:17.680 --> 00:03:19.260
Has something happened?

00:03:19.260 --> 00:03:21.580
Oh, well... actually...

00:03:22.340 --> 00:03:26.440
A friend from school has been nagging me
 about going to a mixer with her.

00:03:26.440 --> 00:03:27.540
A mixer?!

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:28.810
Yeah.

00:03:28.810 --> 00:03:31.040
With college students, apparently.

00:03:31.790 --> 00:03:35.660
Any college student who would intentionally 
go to a mixer with high school girls is—

00:03:35.660 --> 00:03:37.450
Worth giving a chance, don't you think?

00:03:38.780 --> 00:03:41.260
You might find a good partner.

00:03:41.260 --> 00:03:42.070
Oh, please!

00:03:42.550 --> 00:03:44.700
The only reason they're 
inviting a Plain Jane like me

00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:46.570
is to help the other girls look good.

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:48.400
I see.

00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:52.200
A lack of self-awareness 
is both a weapon and a sin.

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:53.090
What?

00:03:53.090 --> 00:03:55.540
Nothing at all.

00:03:56.850 --> 00:03:58.340
Hey, Holmes!

00:03:58.610 --> 00:03:59.860
Akihito-san?

00:03:59.860 --> 00:04:02.540
Hey, Aoi-chan and Rikyu, too!

00:04:02.540 --> 00:04:05.170
Couldn't you enter with a bit more reserve?

00:04:05.170 --> 00:04:06.670
Hey, Holmes...

00:04:06.670 --> 00:04:11.120
Did you get an invitation to 
Yanagihara-sensei's birthday party?

00:04:11.120 --> 00:04:15.230
Yes. Though more precisely, 
it was addressed to my grandfather.

00:04:15.640 --> 00:04:17.610
Yanagihara-sensei?

00:04:17.810 --> 00:04:20.200
He's a famous appraiser.

00:04:20.200 --> 00:04:22.570
He was at the owner's birthday party, too.

00:04:22.570 --> 00:04:24.120
My grandfather will be indisposed,

00:04:24.120 --> 00:04:27.240
so he's asked me to attend in his place.

00:04:27.760 --> 00:04:31.050
I was thinking about 
inviting you along, Aoi-san.

00:04:31.050 --> 00:04:33.370
Hey, I wanna go, too!

00:04:33.660 --> 00:04:37.380
Yanagihara-sensei helped us out 
a lot when my dad died.

00:04:37.380 --> 00:04:39.630
I want to wish him a happy birthday!

00:04:39.910 --> 00:04:41.820
You leave me no choice.

00:04:41.820 --> 00:04:43.840
We'll be a party of three, then.

00:04:43.840 --> 00:04:45.010
Three?!

00:04:45.010 --> 00:04:48.510
What about me, Kiyo-nii? I want to go, too!

00:04:48.770 --> 00:04:51.820
It's not as if we can close the store for it.

00:04:51.820 --> 00:04:53.610
I need to leave Kura in capable hands,

00:04:53.610 --> 00:04:56.120
and you seem to be the best candidate.

00:05:13.500 --> 00:05:16.440
Thank you for coming, Kiyotaka-kun.

00:05:16.440 --> 00:05:18.500
Happy birthday to you.

00:05:19.100 --> 00:05:20.590
Happy birthday!

00:05:21.480 --> 00:05:24.960
My grandfather deeply regrets
 not being able to attend.

00:05:25.560 --> 00:05:30.110
I pulled out all the stops throwin' a party
 to put that old fart to shame.

00:05:30.110 --> 00:05:32.930
Too bad he can't see it for himself.

00:05:34.220 --> 00:05:36.580
But I hope you'll enjoy yourself.

00:05:36.580 --> 00:05:38.120
Your companions, too.

00:05:38.120 --> 00:05:41.690
It's a pleasure to meet you. I'm Mashiro Aoi.

00:05:42.120 --> 00:05:44.100
I'm working part-time at Kura.

00:05:45.000 --> 00:05:49.760
Thank you very much for appraising 
the scrolls my dad left behind.

00:05:50.470 --> 00:05:53.340
Oh, are you Kajiwara-sensei's boy?

00:05:53.340 --> 00:05:55.280
Believe I've seen ya on TV.

00:05:55.280 --> 00:05:56.560
Keep up the good work.

00:05:56.560 --> 00:05:59.590
Y-Yes, sir! Thank you very much!

00:06:00.640 --> 00:06:02.270
Well, you're rather normal.

00:06:07.010 --> 00:06:08.460
<i>Rather normal?</i>

00:06:09.030 --> 00:06:12.710
<i>Does he mean I'm too plain 
to be working at Kura?</i>

00:06:13.530 --> 00:06:16.400
It's because the Yagashira family
 is full of eccentrics.

00:06:17.360 --> 00:06:19.880
He's surprised to see
 a normal girl with the likes of us.

00:06:19.880 --> 00:06:23.980
That's right, Holmes. You're a major weirdo.

00:06:24.280 --> 00:06:27.490
That's profoundly insulting coming from you.

00:06:27.760 --> 00:06:30.800
Though it's preferable to being a boor...

00:06:27.760 --> 00:06:30.800
I think I'm pretty normal myself!

00:06:30.800 --> 00:06:32.870
If I may so rudely interrupt...

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:40.250
We would now like to begin 
the appraising game.

00:06:40.720 --> 00:06:43.250
Appraising game?

00:06:43.790 --> 00:06:45.710
We'll bring out various pieces to view.

00:06:45.710 --> 00:06:48.420
If you think they're real, 
raise the white flag.

00:06:48.420 --> 00:06:52.260
If you think they're fake, 
raise the red flag.

00:06:52.530 --> 00:06:57.580
However, we ask that professional appraisers 
and artists refrain from participating.

00:06:57.580 --> 00:06:59.910
Hey, sounds fun.

00:06:59.910 --> 00:07:01.340
Good luck.

00:07:02.320 --> 00:07:04.770
Now, here's our first item!

00:07:09.740 --> 00:07:12.290
It's a Shigaraki urn!

00:07:16.000 --> 00:07:18.400
It's just a dirty old urn.

00:07:19.790 --> 00:07:20.830
<i>It's true...</i>

00:07:22.120 --> 00:07:25.800
<i>It's so grainy, it just looks like 
 a dirty urn at a glance...</i>

00:07:27.070 --> 00:07:28.170
<i>But...</i>

00:07:30.870 --> 00:07:33.060
<i>This is definitely the real thing.</i>

00:07:34.100 --> 00:07:40.180
Now, let us know what you think.
 Is this Shigaraki urn real or fake?

00:07:46.680 --> 00:07:50.080
Now, Sensei, give us the correct answer!

00:07:51.170 --> 00:07:54.450
This is a genuine Shigaraki urn.

00:07:55.340 --> 00:07:57.430
Y-You gotta be kidding!

00:07:58.430 --> 00:08:02.320
It was made without decoration, 
intended for day-to-day use.

00:08:02.320 --> 00:08:04.930
Well spotted, Aoi-san.

00:08:04.930 --> 00:08:06.300
Y-Yeah!

00:08:06.300 --> 00:08:08.670
You've shown me one like it before, so...

00:08:09.210 --> 00:08:12.220
Now, let's move on to our next item.

00:08:16.990 --> 00:08:18.620
The answer is... red!

00:08:20.630 --> 00:08:21.480
White!

00:08:23.750 --> 00:08:24.920
Red!

00:08:24.920 --> 00:08:27.390
That Kizeto was a fake!

00:08:34.960 --> 00:08:39.640
Now for the final test 
between our last two contestants!

00:08:42.370 --> 00:08:44.750
<i>That's a Shino tea bowl!</i>

00:08:49.360 --> 00:08:51.600
<i>That's one piece I'd recognize anywhere.</i>

00:08:52.330 --> 00:08:56.010
Now, it's time to decide!

00:08:56.490 --> 00:08:58.850
Your answers, please!

00:09:04.000 --> 00:09:05.400
They're split!

00:09:10.520 --> 00:09:12.810
Sensei, please do the honors.

00:09:15.630 --> 00:09:16.890
My lady...

00:09:16.890 --> 00:09:19.980
You are superbly discerning.

00:09:21.240 --> 00:09:22.660
This one's a fake.

00:09:25.920 --> 00:09:26.980
Aoi-san!

00:09:29.750 --> 00:09:30.670
Holmes-san!

00:09:31.230 --> 00:09:32.630
Aoi-san.

00:09:32.630 --> 00:09:36.880
I knew from the start 
that you had a good eye.

00:09:39.180 --> 00:09:43.280
I-It's only because you showed 
me all those things...

00:09:43.280 --> 00:09:44.180
Hardly.

00:09:44.690 --> 00:09:50.970
It's because you're the kind of person 
who never averts your eyes from the truth.

00:09:50.970 --> 00:09:52.900
Congratulations.

00:09:52.900 --> 00:09:57.280
You win a trip for two at 
Kinosaki Inn's Tsukimiya suite.

00:09:57.280 --> 00:09:59.700
F-For two?!

00:09:59.700 --> 00:10:02.210
You can go with Kiyotaka-kun!

00:09:59.700 --> 00:10:03.580
<b>Winner</b>

00:10:03.790 --> 00:10:05.600
What?!

00:10:10.570 --> 00:10:15.590
You've all been very discerning so far,

00:10:15.590 --> 00:10:19.090
but today's event isn't over yet.

00:10:19.090 --> 00:10:25.180
We would now like a certain young 
appraiser to take a look at this work!

00:10:27.470 --> 00:10:33.360
It's a piece by English painter 
William Holman Hunt, <i>Our English Coasts</i>.

00:10:34.170 --> 00:10:36.970
Is it real or fake,

00:10:36.970 --> 00:10:38.220
Kiyotaka-kun?

00:10:39.690 --> 00:10:42.120
Can you tell us?

00:10:47.040 --> 00:10:47.870
Very well.

00:11:07.970 --> 00:11:10.530
<i>He usually identifies things right away...</i>

00:11:24.810 --> 00:11:26.860
It's very skillfully painted.

00:11:28.180 --> 00:11:29.260
But it's a counterfeit...

00:11:30.140 --> 00:11:31.500
Isn't it?

00:11:32.820 --> 00:11:34.460
What makes you think that?

00:11:36.460 --> 00:11:40.420
I've heard that this painting 
brought Hunt great distinction.

00:11:40.910 --> 00:11:44.720
It's said to be one of the best 
depictions of natural light ever.

00:11:45.970 --> 00:11:48.500
But when I look at this...

00:11:48.500 --> 00:11:52.190
I feel none of the natural 
magnificence of sunlight.

00:11:53.210 --> 00:11:56.170
Therefore, I believe it's a counterfeit.

00:12:05.040 --> 00:12:06.700
Splendidly done.

00:12:06.940 --> 00:12:11.860
You're correct. This is a forgery 
lent to me by a gallery.

00:12:17.440 --> 00:12:18.800
Yanagihara-sensei.

00:12:20.570 --> 00:12:26.840
Could I ask you the name of the gallery 
employee who lent you this painting?

00:12:29.340 --> 00:12:32.220
I believe it was... Moria.

00:12:33.680 --> 00:12:34.580
Moria?

00:12:35.800 --> 00:12:36.740
Sensei.

00:12:37.850 --> 00:12:42.660
Was it him that asked you 
to have me look at this Hunt painting?

00:12:43.150 --> 00:12:43.990
No.

00:12:44.440 --> 00:12:47.860
He didn't ask for you by name.

00:12:47.860 --> 00:12:51.820
He simply said "your youngest appraiser."

00:12:52.380 --> 00:12:54.500
And if you were correct,

00:12:54.830 --> 00:12:56.750
he asked for me...

00:12:56.750 --> 00:12:58.590
to give you this.

00:12:58.590 --> 00:12:59.250
Here.

00:13:05.440 --> 00:13:07.960
Holmes! Hey, Holmes!

00:13:08.510 --> 00:13:09.850
Holmes-san!

00:13:09.850 --> 00:13:11.850
What's going on with you?

00:13:15.170 --> 00:13:17.030
"Moria," my ass!

00:13:17.030 --> 00:13:18.020
He's screwin' with me!

00:13:18.970 --> 00:13:22.510
Seriously... what's wrong?

00:13:26.040 --> 00:13:29.620
Ensho was the one who arranged that forgery.

00:13:32.360 --> 00:13:34.920
Though it seems he's calling himself Moria.

00:13:34.920 --> 00:13:38.170
Like Moriarty! Holmes's rival!

00:13:39.490 --> 00:13:42.740
And then he sent me this round mirror.

00:13:42.740 --> 00:13:46.420
He's saying, "If you can figure 
out where I am, come find me."

00:13:46.780 --> 00:13:48.760
Where is he, though?

00:13:51.100 --> 00:13:52.520
Genko-an Temple.

00:13:55.500 --> 00:13:58.730
The Window of Enlightenment 
and the Window of Straying?

00:13:59.320 --> 00:14:02.190
The round mirror represents 
the Window of Enlightenment.

00:14:02.750 --> 00:14:10.790
And Hunt's <i>Our English Coasts </i>
is also known as <i>Strayed Sheep</i>.

00:14:11.380 --> 00:14:13.590
And that led you to the Window of Straying?

00:14:14.920 --> 00:14:17.710
<i></i>Strayed... Sheep<i>?</i>

00:14:19.850 --> 00:14:22.690
But... no one's here.

00:14:23.560 --> 00:14:25.350
You sure this is the place?

00:14:26.420 --> 00:14:29.650
At any rate, we should pay
 our respects while we're here.

00:14:36.510 --> 00:14:38.600
Good to see you here.

00:14:40.480 --> 00:14:42.430
You're the one who called me here.

00:14:47.540 --> 00:14:48.970
Sure am.

00:14:48.970 --> 00:14:50.490
When did he...

00:14:51.000 --> 00:14:53.990
<i>Is that Ensho?</i>

00:14:54.400 --> 00:14:58.390
Now, the real question is... 
was I hopin' you'd come or not?

00:15:04.250 --> 00:15:06.980
I can't say I knew for sure myself.

00:15:09.410 --> 00:15:10.520
Then...

00:15:11.890 --> 00:15:13.400
How do you feel now?

00:15:16.470 --> 00:15:19.710
What was it that gave my work away?

00:15:21.120 --> 00:15:22.270
The light.

00:15:24.860 --> 00:15:27.900
I see. The light, eh?

00:15:30.990 --> 00:15:37.040
It ain't easy for a man livin' in the 
shadows to depict light, I guess.

00:15:39.440 --> 00:15:44.060
It was very clever of you 
to choose a place like this.

00:15:44.750 --> 00:15:46.070
Much obliged.

00:15:47.440 --> 00:15:51.920
The Window of Straying represents 
human existence and mortal suffering.

00:15:52.680 --> 00:15:58.560
The Window of Enlightenment represents 
the zen mindset and the greater universe.

00:15:59.410 --> 00:16:04.170
I did enjoy the time 
I spent waitin' for you here.

00:16:04.170 --> 00:16:08.310
Almost like waitin' to see an old flame.

00:16:08.310 --> 00:16:11.700
I'm not exactly pleased to hear that.

00:16:13.750 --> 00:16:20.200
Plenty of counterfeiters leave 
their own mark on their works.

00:16:21.080 --> 00:16:27.210
Before now, I never could 
figure out why they'd do that.

00:16:28.010 --> 00:16:31.460
I came from a single-parent 
household, you see...

00:16:31.810 --> 00:16:34.180
My dad was a painter.

00:16:34.720 --> 00:16:37.920
Whenever he couldn't finish by a deadline,

00:16:37.920 --> 00:16:40.160
I'd start takin' over.

00:16:42.010 --> 00:16:46.050
My dad praised me lots for that.

00:16:47.250 --> 00:16:50.230
That's when I first took up counterfeitin'.

00:16:50.660 --> 00:16:54.550
But then my dad died, 
I got bored with counterfeitin',

00:16:54.550 --> 00:16:56.540
and I joined the priesthood.

00:16:56.540 --> 00:16:58.990
I thought I'd retired for good.

00:16:59.990 --> 00:17:03.870
His emotional instability originated 
with experiences in his childhood.

00:17:03.870 --> 00:17:07.880
And a close family member... 
his father, perhaps, was an artist.

00:17:08.400 --> 00:17:12.020
Inspired by this person, 
Ensho pursued the path of art.

00:17:12.020 --> 00:17:15.880
His father realized his talent and 
encouraged him to produce counterfeits.

00:17:16.860 --> 00:17:18.920
<i>Just like Holmes said...</i>

00:17:20.220 --> 00:17:21.390
But then...

00:17:22.370 --> 00:17:27.100
You saw through works of mine 
that no one ever had before,

00:17:27.100 --> 00:17:28.650
and it set my heart racin'.

00:17:31.610 --> 00:17:34.650
My heart was racin' this time, too.

00:17:34.650 --> 00:17:36.240
See through it...

00:17:36.240 --> 00:17:37.410
Don't see through it...

00:17:37.640 --> 00:17:38.660
Come to me...

00:17:38.660 --> 00:17:40.910
Don't come to me, I thought...

00:17:42.730 --> 00:17:43.910
But...

00:17:44.480 --> 00:17:47.920
When you asked how I felt just now,
 I knew for sure...

00:17:59.780 --> 00:18:01.120
That could have been serious.

00:18:05.030 --> 00:18:07.910
I really don't think I like ya.

00:18:08.820 --> 00:18:10.600
The feelin' is mutual.

00:18:10.600 --> 00:18:12.940
I don't like you... either!

00:18:14.870 --> 00:18:17.500
Seems I can't retire just yet.

00:18:18.340 --> 00:18:22.820
Not until I make ya suffer
 unbelievable humiliation...

00:18:23.450 --> 00:18:26.000
I have no intention of being humiliated.

00:18:26.000 --> 00:18:27.460
I would prefer it if you'd refrain.

00:18:28.550 --> 00:18:30.460
Oh, I'm just quakin'.

00:18:31.290 --> 00:18:33.210
Hey, ya heard this one before?

00:18:33.210 --> 00:18:35.960
There's bloodstains on the ceilin' here.

00:18:36.980 --> 00:18:37.980
Where?

00:18:38.580 --> 00:18:39.970
Is that them?

00:18:40.400 --> 00:18:42.220
Old footprints...

00:18:42.220 --> 00:18:44.260
Was there a ninja or something?!

00:18:49.830 --> 00:18:52.570
He's much like a ninja himself.

00:18:53.080 --> 00:18:55.220
The reason there are 
footprints on the ceiling here

00:18:55.220 --> 00:18:59.250
is because the ceiling was built with
 floorboards from Fushimi-Momoyama Castle.

00:19:02.140 --> 00:19:03.530
That reprehensible man...

00:19:08.500 --> 00:19:10.790
"Victory"? What the heck?!

00:19:08.500 --> 00:19:14.000
<b>Victory</b>

00:19:10.790 --> 00:19:12.670
Holmes was the winner here!

00:19:12.670 --> 00:19:14.000
That's right!

00:19:15.190 --> 00:19:16.340
You're wrong.

00:19:17.490 --> 00:19:19.060
I didn't see through him.

00:19:19.960 --> 00:19:23.260
I only got the right answer 
usin' the knowledge that I have.

00:19:24.910 --> 00:19:27.020
I lost this round.

00:19:27.390 --> 00:19:29.430
The moment I said the light
 was what gave it away...

00:19:30.270 --> 00:19:33.770
he smiled like he'd won.

00:19:36.640 --> 00:19:37.220
But...

00:19:37.220 --> 00:19:39.150
He did win.

00:19:39.990 --> 00:19:41.390
An' I lost.

00:19:41.960 --> 00:19:43.390
<i>That's not true!</i>

00:19:44.510 --> 00:19:46.400
<i>Holmes-san won here!</i>

00:19:46.400 --> 00:19:47.960
<i>His knowledge was just a part of that!</i>

00:19:49.700 --> 00:19:50.740
<i>No...</i>

00:19:51.270 --> 00:19:55.170
<i>What Holmes-san needs 
right now isn't comfort.</i>

00:19:56.080 --> 00:19:57.420
In that case...

00:19:58.190 --> 00:20:01.420
In that case, the next time 
Ensho challenges you...

00:20:01.420 --> 00:20:03.420
See through him, okay?

00:20:05.220 --> 00:20:08.610
Next time... don't lose to him!

00:20:11.160 --> 00:20:12.200
Aoi-san...

00:20:17.040 --> 00:20:19.190
Yes, I'll do just that.

00:20:20.950 --> 00:20:22.310
Holmes-san!

00:20:29.150 --> 00:20:32.620
Hey, now. Forgive me for scarin' ya, all right?

00:20:35.840 --> 00:20:37.140
I'm okay.

00:20:54.940 --> 00:20:59.230
<i>Maybe Ensho chose this place because 
he felt astray in the world...</i>

00:21:00.190 --> 00:21:05.100
<i>And in the end, he chose to follow 
his desire to destroy Holmes-san...</i>

00:21:06.320 --> 00:21:07.250
Aoi-san.

00:21:08.540 --> 00:21:11.190
Thank you for before.

00:21:12.240 --> 00:21:14.100
I'm going to get better

00:21:14.100 --> 00:21:18.000
and become the kind of connoisseur 
who can see through any counterfeit.

00:21:20.560 --> 00:21:21.380
Okay!

00:21:25.100 --> 00:21:26.260
Aoi-san.

00:21:26.460 --> 00:21:28.510
Y-Yes?

00:21:30.420 --> 00:21:30.970
I...

00:21:30.970 --> 00:21:33.810
Hey! Are you guys coming or not?

00:21:35.360 --> 00:21:38.410
Well... I'm sorry.

00:21:38.410 --> 00:21:40.770
I hope we'll get a chance to talk later.

00:21:41.070 --> 00:21:42.900
When Akihito-san isn't around.

00:21:43.720 --> 00:21:45.280
R-Right...

00:21:50.530 --> 00:21:51.630
Shall we, then?

00:21:52.240 --> 00:21:53.290
Yeah.

00:22:07.320 --> 00:22:14.290
<b>Holmes of Kyoto</b>

00:23:36.390 --> 00:23:51.400
Christmas Eve Tears and a Broken Alibi

00:23:36.390 --> 00:23:51.400
Next Episode

00:23:37.000 --> 00:23:38.500
The Christmas season...

00:23:38.500 --> 00:23:39.850
My heart seems to be raging

00:23:39.850 --> 00:23:41.260
like a winter storm.

00:23:41.260 --> 00:23:42.560
A fine senryu poem.

00:23:42.560 --> 00:23:43.120
What?!

00:23:43.120 --> 00:23:44.980
You heard that?

00:23:44.980 --> 00:23:48.710
Next time: "Christmas Eve 
Tears and a Broken Alibi."

00:23:48.710 --> 00:23:51.020
Holmes-san, you really are nasty.
